{"uid":"28c65ae429b2090a","name":"test_concurrent_conflicting_deliveries_converge_without_corruption","fullName":"tests.webhook.test_ordering#test_concurrent_conflicting_deliveries_converge_without_corruption","time":{"start":1787290223386,"stop":1787290223420,"duration":34},"description":"Five contradictory events at one payment, fired at once, no sequencing.\n\nThis is the case BEGIN IMMEDIATE and WAL exist for. Each delivery reads the\ncurrent state and writes the next one, and without the write lock taken up\nfront those two steps interleave and a higher rank gets overwritten by a\nlower one that read stale state.\n\nThe expected state is refunded because it is the highest rank in the set,\nand that expectation does not depend on who wins any race: the rule is\nmonotonic, so whatever order the threads land in, rank 80 is applied and\nnothing below it can replace it. A test that accepted several states would\nbe asserting almost nothing, which is why this asserts exactly one.\n\nA \"database is locked\" failure here is a WAL problem from stage 01, not a\nstate machine problem. That distinction is why WAL was set up there.\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>Five contradictory events at one payment, fired at once, no sequencing.</p>\n<p>This is the case BEGIN IMMEDIATE and WAL exist for. Each delivery reads the<br />\ncurrent state and writes the next one, and without the write lock taken up<br />\nfront those two steps interleave and a higher rank gets overwritten by a<br />\nlower one that read stale state.</p>\n<p>The expected state is refunded because it is the highest rank in the set,<br />\nand that expectation does not depend on who wins any race: the rule is<br />\nmonotonic, so whatever order the threads land in, rank 80 is applied and<br />\nnothing below it can replace it. A test that accepted several states would<br />\nbe asserting almost nothing, which is why this asserts exactly one.</p>\n<p>A &quot;database is locked&quot; failure here is a WAL problem from s